# Commits and push

## Commits
1. Commit every decision you make about the project, locally, as soon as the step is done. Never skip or postpone a commit, and do not ask for permission to commit.
2. Commit messages are in English only and follow Conventional Commits. The detailed steps are in `10-git-discipline.mdc`.

## Push — the agent never pushes
3. The person always pushes from their own terminal.
4. When something should go online, print this command for the person to run:
   ```
   PUSH_OK=1 git push origin <branch>
   ```
   The remote `origin` has two push URLs, so this one command reaches both hosts:
   - GitHub: `https://github.com/evaaliya/developing_with_qnx`
   - GitLab: `https://gitlab.com/evaaliya/developing_with_qnx`
5. After the person has pushed, and if they ask, read back both hosts (`git ls-remote github` and `git ls-remote gitlab`) and report what each one holds.
6. Never add or change a remote on your own.
